abstract: >-
  Python code accompanying the manuscript "Incremental value of large language
  model-extracted discharge-summary flags for antimicrobial resistance
  prediction: a retrospective cohort study with temporal validation in an
  Indian tertiary-care hospital" (submitted to BMC Medical Informatics and
  Decision Making). The scripts cover de-identification, cohort construction
  and labelling of MRSA, ESBL and CRE, structured feature engineering,
  rule-based and large language model (Claude Sonnet 5) extraction of 13
  clinical flags from discharge summaries, physician-validation sampling and
  scoring, model development (logistic regression, random forest, XGBoost)
  with a calendar-ordered, patient-exclusive temporal split, patient-cluster
  bootstrap comparisons with multiplicity correction, recalibration, decision
  curve analysis, SHAP, subgroup, decomposition and sensitivity analyses,
  data-quality checks, and generation of all tables and figures. Patient-level
  data are not included; see the README for the expected inputs and run order.
keywords:
  - antimicrobial resistance
  - large language models
  - clinical natural language processing
  - prediction model
  - temporal validation
  - India
